# Third-party components

KGtechvault is built on third-party open-source software, each component
licensed by its own authors under its own terms. Nothing in LICENSE restricts
rights you hold in those components, and nothing here grants rights in
KGtechvault itself.

This file names the dependency sets and where their exact, pinned versions and
licences are recorded, rather than restating licence texts that would drift out
of date the first time a lock file moves.

| Set | Manifest | Pinned at |
|---|---|---|
| Backend runtime (Python) | `KG_backend/requirements.txt` | `ops/docker/backend-requirements.lock` |
| Frontend runtime and build (Node) | `kg_frontend/package.json` | `kg_frontend/package-lock.json` |
| Browser test suite | `qa/e2e/package.json` | `qa/e2e/package-lock.json` |
| Base images | `ops/docker/backend.Dockerfile`, `ops/docker/frontend.Dockerfile` | image digests resolved at build |
| Observability and error tracking | `ops/observability/docker-compose.yml`, `glitchtip` compose on the host | image tags in those files |

The principal components, named because they shape the architecture rather than
because the list is exhaustive: Django, Next.js and React, PostgreSQL, SQLite
(with `sqlite-vec`), sentence-transformers and PyTorch, BAAI `bge-m3`,
WeasyPrint, nginx, Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, Grafana Alloy, cAdvisor,
GlitchTip, Umami, Playwright, k6, OWASP ZAP, Trivy, gitleaks, bandit and
hadolint.

To reproduce the full licence inventory for an audit:

```bash
pip install pip-licenses && pip-licenses --from=mixed --format=markdown   # Python
npm --prefix kg_frontend ls --all --long --json                          # Node
docker run --rm aquasec/trivy:0.58.1 image --scanners license <image>    # images
```

Model weights are downloaded at build time from their publishers and are
covered by those publishers' terms; `HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1` in CI and in the
production images means no component fetches weights at runtime.
